$ yo effects --help
Usage: yo effects <file-or-dir> [options]

Report which effect capabilities each EXPORTED top-level fn requires, read
off the function types the type checker computed: a parameter whose type is
a handler record (a struct with a ctl(...) field — Exception,
ResumableException(T)) is kind 'ctl'; the prelude Io is kind 'io'; an
effects-row implicit is kind 'row'. Bundles such as IoExn report every
member's kind. A returned Impl(Future(T, E)) reports E under 'future'.
A fn with no effect parameters is pure with respect to capabilities.

Options:
  --json                    One JSON object per module: {"file", "functions":
                            [{"name", "effects": [{"param", "type", "via",
                            "kinds"}]}]}
  --exclude <path>          Exclude a directory/file (repeatable)
  --std-path <dir>          Override the std library directory

Examples:
  $ yo effects ./src
  $ yo effects main.yo --json
